# Security Analysis: In-Memory Loader

## Memory Protection Mechanisms
- Uses mmap() with PROT_EXEC for executable memory allocation
- Implements proper memory cleanup with munmap()
- Avoids disk-based payload storage

## Detection Evasion Techniques
- No file system artifacts created
- Direct memory execution without intermediate files
- Dynamic memory allocation patterns

## Potential Detection Points
- Memory allocation with RWX permissions
- Unusual memory mapping patterns
- System call sequences (mmap, memcpy, execution)

## Mitigation Recommendations
- Monitor mmap() calls with executable permissions
- Implement Control Flow Integrity (CFI)
- Use Address Space Layout Randomization (ASLR)
Subtask 5.2: Document Loader Architecture
